{
  "name": "Decode HTML entities",
  "description": "Reverse HTML entity encoding: named entities (&amp; &lt; &copy; and many more), decimal numeric entities (&#8364;), and hex numeric entities (&#x1F600;) all become their characters. An unknown &name; is left as-is. Useful for turning scraped or exported HTML back into plain text. The inverse of html-escape.",
  "summary": "Decode HTML entities to characters",
